  "text_md": "![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nNAVWEPS 00-802-30 SELECTED REFERENCES\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile2.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile3.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile4.png>)\n\n# SELECTEDREFERENCES\n\n- 1. Dommasch, Sherby, and Connolly “Airplane Aerodynamics” Pitman Publishing Co. 2d Edition, 1957\n- 2. Perkins and Hage “Airplane Performance, Stability, and Control” John Wiley and Sons\n\n- 1949\n\n3. E. A. Bonney “Engineering Supersonic Aerodynamics” McGraw-Hill Book Co.\n\n- 1950\n\n\n- 4. Hurt, Vernon, and Martin “Aeronautical Engineering, Section I, Manual of Instruction, Avi-\n\nation Safety Officer Course” University of Southern California\n\n- 1958\n\n5. Fairchild, Magill, and Brye “Principles of Helicopter Engineering” University of Southern California\n\n- 1959\n\n\n\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile5.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile6.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile7.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile8.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile9.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile10.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile11.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile12.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0843_images/imageFile13.png>)\n\n![](<3de34e2ac095df7c0650dfb82b97c4b4a76b43568aa70cf50819d17fd1ca0